<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 183 0 R/T(CONCLUSION )/E(CONCLUSION )/Pg 26 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

460 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 183 0 R/E(Space systems are part of daily life. GPS, banking, and flights all depend on satellites working safely.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

461 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 183 0 R/E(Every part of the system can be attacked \204 space, ground, or the user side. That's why encryption alone is not enough. We also need authentication, so unauthorized commands can be rejected.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

462 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 183 0 R/E(These are not just theory. Black Sea already showed us this risk is real.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

463 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 183 0 R/E(Frameworks like NIST, CCSDS, ISO, and ECSS give us a standard to follow. And recovery plans matter just as much as prevention, because attacks can still happen even with good security.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

